# CODEOWNERS — coverage model (un-inverted).
#
# DEFAULT = UNOWNED: any path not matched below needs no code-owner review, so a
# low-risk deterministic PR (and a Margot LOW-risk verdict) can merge without the
# operator. There is deliberately NO `* @owner` catch-all.
#
# OWNED (listed below) = paths where a JUDGMENT change must have a human: the
# safety / identity / gate machinery. The branch ruleset requires code-owner
# review (with 0 baseline approvals), so touching any owned path holds the PR for
# @lexijamesesq; touching only unowned paths does not.
#
# When adding a path: uncertain -> OWNED (under-coverage — an owned path left
# unowned — is the dangerous direction). Prefer anchored patterns (/path/ or
# /file) over bare names: a bare name matches at any depth and can clear or claim
# more than a reviewer expects.

# --- Gate machinery (the CI/gate/hook chain and its configs) ---
/.github/workflows/            @lexijamesesq
/.github/actions/              @lexijamesesq
/.github/scripts/              @lexijamesesq
/.github/zizmor.yml            @lexijamesesq
/.github/dependabot.yml        @lexijamesesq
/.pre-commit-config.yaml       @lexijamesesq
/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml        @lexijamesesq
/git-hooks/                    @lexijamesesq
/drift-check-report.sh         @lexijamesesq

# --- Gate/lint configs that can DISABLE a check (gate self-protection) ---
/.gitleaks.toml                @lexijamesesq
/.vale.ini                     @lexijamesesq
/styles/Estate/                @lexijamesesq
/.shellcheckrc                 @lexijamesesq

# --- The gate's own PROOF (a test change can silently weaken a required check) ---
/.claude/eval/                 @lexijamesesq

# --- PR-body gate input (machine-parsed by the pr-body check) ---
/.github/pull_request_template.md   @lexijamesesq

# --- Governance & policy ---
/.claude/rules/                @lexijamesesq
/.claude/settings.json         @lexijamesesq
/rulesets/                     @lexijamesesq
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @lexijamesesq

# --- Credentials & trust boundaries: covered by /.gitleaks.toml + /git-hooks/ above ---

# --- Release / identity / bootstrap wiring ---
/setup-claude-profiles.sh      @lexijamesesq
/setup-terminal.sh             @lexijamesesq

